  "question": {
    "html": "<p>The frequency of a mass-spring system oscillating horizontally with simple harmonic motion (SHM) on the surface of planet X is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"f\"></span>. The gravitational field strength at the surface of planet X is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"g_{X}\"></span>. The mass-spring system is moved to the surface of planet Y where the gravitational field strength is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"g_{Y}\"></span>. <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{g_{X}}{g_{Y}}=\\frac{1}{4}\"></span>. What is the frequency at which the mass-spring system oscillates on the surface of planet Y?</p>\n<p></p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\">\n<li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{f}{2}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"f\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2f\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"D\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"4f\"></span></li>\n</ol>"
  },
